= Overview
The FIRMUPS solution outlined in the previous project work @project-work-firmups defines a clear architecture of an update solution for embedded devices. This chapter focuses on integrating the requirements elaborated in the prestudy in #ref(<prestudy>) into the architecture and design of the solution. The main focus is in accordance with the scientific question on the ability of the solution to accommodate different connectivity types as well as the scalability capabilities of the solution. The architecture and design decisions are documented using #gls("adr", first: false)s based on the markdown #gls("adr", first: false) templates from @adr-github. The decisions are based on the prestudy done in the previous project work as well as on further research and analysis done for this chapter.

